  "notes": "This is a methodology/statistics paper showing that stochastic fluctuations of bosonic dark matter (VULF) require relaxing previously published constraints by factors of ~3-10 for experiments in the T<<tau_c regime. It does not present a new independent exclusion limit but rather applies correction factors to existing limits (CASPEr-ZULF, nEDM, dilaton clock searches). The modified exclusion plots (Figs 3, 4) are re-derivations of others' limits, not numerical tables. No extractable new data points. The paper discusses both axion-nucleon (gaNN) and scalar/dilaton (d_e) couplings, so coupling type is ambiguous. Local DM density rho_DM ~ 0.4 GeV/cm^3 is mentioned. | Vision: Black solid line traces the combined CASPEr-ZULF Comagnetometer + nEDM exclusion boundary on the g_aNN axion-nucleon coupling plot. The upper boundary (high coupling) is excluded above. The boundary starts ~1e-3 at m=1e-22 eV, dips to a minimum ~3.6e-2 (deepest exclusion) around 1e-19 to 1e-18 eV, then rises back up near 1e-17 eV. Note: y-axis is g_aNN in GeV^-1 but mapped to AxionNeutron coupling type. Data approximate from reading the black contour. | CV axis calibration succeeded (ranges consistent with LLM) | Curve traced by classical CV | Calibration: No calibration needed",
